<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18234" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fissĭlis</span></b> , e, adj.
		findo. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>That may be cleft</i> or <i>split</i>, <i>fissile</i> (rare; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">not in Cic. or Caes.): robur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 6, 181</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lignum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. G.
					1, 144</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Plin. 16, 39, 73, § 187</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">arundo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					16, 36, 64, § 157</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vena lapidis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					36, 17, 27, § 131</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Cleft</i>, <i>split</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">stipes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					9, 1, 3</span></i>
			. —Comically transf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ad focum si adesses, Non fissile haberes caput,</span>”
				<i>you would not have had your crown cracked</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Aul. 3, 2, 26</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
